{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785236276,"nonce":"1/cpsoYkb3Kl1U73NYBfqY4xetQ=","title":"ADR-0062: a content identity costs an identity walk of the untouched tree, which part 3 does not book","message":"ADR-0062 part 3 says the drain \"hashes only those files\" in the change set. That is true of the **snapshot root** and false of the **content identity**, and the difference was found while implementing the fold (`crates/scarab-server/src/settle.rs`).\n\nA content identity is *not an address* — nothing is stored under one and nothing can be fetched by one (CONTEXT.md §4.2). So an untouched subtree that the fold carries forward **by hash** has a known root and an **unknown identity**. Every rebuilt directory level must therefore walk its untouched sibling subtrees to compute theirs: one `tree_entries` per directory, recursively.\n\nThe consequence is shaped opposite to intuition. A change deep in the tree is cheap. **A change near the root costs an identity walk of most of the parent tree** — so editing `README.md` at the workspace root is the expensive case, not editing one file under `target/`.\n\nThis is local work against the warm tier, so part 3's \"no network in the path\" claim stands unharmed. The claim that does not stand is \"hashes only those files\", and the cost is currently unbooked in an ADR whose whole argument is about per-file cost.\n\nMemoised within a single fold in `settle.rs`, which bounds it to one walk per directory rather than one per reference. That is a constant-factor fix, not a structural one.\n\nThe structural fix is an **identity index in the warm tier**: a persisted `snapshot root -\u003e content identity` map, so a carried subtree's identity is a lookup instead of a walk. The warm tier already holds the trees; it does not hold this.\n\n- [ ] Measure it first: identity-walk `tree_entries` calls for a root-level edit vs a deep edit, on a tree with a realistic `target/`-shaped subtree. A fix for an unmeasured cost is how ADR-0061's premise got inverted.\n- [ ] Decide whether the index is worth a persisted store or whether the memoised walk is adequate at real tree sizes\n- [ ] Amend ADR-0062 part 3's \"hashes only those files\" wording either way","files":null}]}